<section id="faq">
  <span class="sec-num" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="sec-tag rv">Questions</span>
    <h2 class="rv">Asked before buying.</h2>
    <div class="faq rv">
      <details>
        <summary>What is BotBento: Content Box?</summary>
        <p>A workflow kit for creators and marketers: 20 AI mini-agent workflow cards across planning, drafting, repurposing, audience and publishing ops — plus a voice guide system built from your own best work, a dated 2026 disclosure-rules reference with sources, the offline Hook Lab checker, trackers and a Notion database. Each card gives the AI a job, your material, your voice, a review step and a next action.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will platforms punish me for using AI?</summary>
        <p>Platforms punish mass-produced minimal-human-input content and unlabeled realistic synthetic media — not AI-assisted work. AI-written hooks, scripts and captions are explicitly exempt from labels on the major platforms, and content that passes human editorial review sits in the EU AI Act's disclosure carve-out. The review-first loop in this box is exactly the pattern the rules reward.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need code, APIs or automation tools?</summary>
        <p>No. The cards run inside the AI chat assistant you already use, and Hook Lab is a single file that opens in any browser and works offline. Nothing to install, no accounts to create.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will it still sound like me?</summary>
